{
  "source": "Prompts/critical-thinking-v14.mp4",
  "duration": 186.4533125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.1,
      "text": "Look at the left side."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.6,
      "end": 3.08,
      "text": "Knowledge forms your baseline."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.7,
      "end": 5.4,
      "text": "It helps you understand a subject"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.4,
      "end": 8.32,
      "text": "and recognize when something in a text or a prompt"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.32,
      "end": 9.2,
      "text": "doesn't add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.8,
      "end": 11.74,
      "text": "On the right side is the active component."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.38,
      "end": 14.58,
      "text": "Critical thinking means you question a claim,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.98,
      "end": 16.78,
      "text": "examine the evidence, and consider"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.78,
      "end": 20.22,
      "text": "alternative explanations before you decide what to do next."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.94,
      "end": 22.56,
      "text": "When you combine these two halves,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.0,
      "end": 25.84,
      "text": "the result is better questions and better decisions."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.46,
      "end": 27.86,
      "text": "Be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.86,
      "end": 30.38,
      "text": "It isn't don't trust anything either."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.52,
      "end": 33.56,
      "text": "It's the habit of asking what would have to be true"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.56,
      "end": 34.98,
      "text": "for a claim to hold up."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.98,
      "end": 39.1,
      "text": "In 2015, news outlets around the world"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.1,
      "end": 41.5,
      "text": "published stories about a scientific study"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.5,
      "end": 44.48,
      "text": "claiming a delicious new method for losing weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.08,
      "end": 47.96,
      "text": "One front page ran the headline, slim by chocolate."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.58,
      "end": 50.66,
      "text": "The face value reaction was immediate."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.18,
      "end": 51.72,
      "text": "Sounds great."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.36,
      "end": 55.34,
      "text": "I believe it, but a critical thinking reaction"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.34,
      "end": 56.4,
      "text": "takes a different path."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.4,
      "end": 58.94,
      "text": "Wait, what's behind the claim?"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.52,
      "end": 61.36,
      "text": "You must force yourself to pause,"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.76,
      "end": 64.46,
      "text": "especially when a claim matches what you want to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.22,
      "end": 67.14,
      "text": "The study itself actually existed."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.68,
      "end": 69.58,
      "text": "However, it was deliberately designed"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.58,
      "end": 71.12,
      "text": "to be scientifically flimsy."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.88,
      "end": 74.86,
      "text": "This diagram illustrates the primary flaw in the data."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.42,
      "end": 77.74,
      "text": "The researchers used a tiny sample size"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.74,
      "end": 79.38,
      "text": "of only 15 participants,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.52,
      "end": 82.56,
      "text": "but they tracked 18 entirely different measurements"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.56,
      "end": 83.5,
      "text": "for each person."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.84,
      "end": 86.38,
      "text": "With that many measurements in such a small group,"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.8,
      "end": 89.24,
      "text": "a chance result could look like an important discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.08,
      "end": 92.68,
      "text": "The supposed research institute backing the study"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.68,
      "end": 94.98,
      "text": "was nothing more than a fabricated website."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.7,
      "end": 97.14,
      "text": "The true author was a journalist."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.74,
      "end": 99.48,
      "text": "He orchestrated the entire stunt"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.48,
      "end": 101.0,
      "text": "to prove that bad science"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.0,
      "end": 102.88,
      "text": "wrapped in a highly appealing headline"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.88,
      "end": 106.02,
      "text": "will spread globally before anyone verifies the facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.74,
      "end": 108.6,
      "text": "Critical thinking requires the ability"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.6,
      "end": 110.36,
      "text": "to read between those lines,"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.76,
      "end": 113.24,
      "text": "particularly when our desires make us vulnerable"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.24,
      "end": 114.66,
      "text": "to confirmation bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.76,
      "end": 118.26,
      "text": "This board outlines five habits you can build"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.26,
      "end": 119.38,
      "text": "to sharpen your thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.04,
      "end": 122.5,
      "text": "Every single one functions as a direct question."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.18,
      "end": 125.1,
      "text": "Habit one, is it actually right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.66,
      "end": 127.5,
      "text": "You check what evidence supports the claim"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.5,
      "end": 129.0,
      "text": "and verify if that evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.0,
      "end": 130.74,
      "text": "genuinely aligns with the conclusion."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.5,
      "end": 133.54,
      "text": "Habit two, do I know enough to judge?"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.02,
      "end": 136.52,
      "text": "You have to recognize the limits of your own knowledge"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.52,
      "end": 139.12,
      "text": "and identify exactly what you still need to learn."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.8,
      "end": 141.24,
      "text": "Habit three, what's missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.6,
      "end": 144.0,
      "text": "You actively hunt for omitted information"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.0,
      "end": 145.68,
      "text": "or alternative explanation."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.48,
      "end": 148.04,
      "text": "Fourth, why am I convinced?"
    },
    {
      "start": 148.74,
      "end": 149.84,
      "text": "Question your own motives"
    },
    {
      "start": 149.84,
      "end": 151.96,
      "text": "to see if you are swayed by hard evidence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 152.34,
      "end": 154.4,
      "text": "confident wording or wishful thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.02,
      "end": 156.66,
      "text": "And fifth, what's my call?"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.3,
      "end": 159.48,
      "text": "Finally, you decide what to believe or do,"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.82,
      "end": 161.72,
      "text": "keeping the flexibility to change your mind"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.72,
      "end": 162.56,
      "text": "when you learn more."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.22,
      "end": 166.04,
      "text": "These five questions work on any information you consume."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.46,
      "end": 168.1,
      "text": "They are especially critical"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.1,
      "end": 170.16,
      "text": "when you use artificial intelligence."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.76,
      "end": 173.06,
      "text": "AI can help you find a flaw in your thinking"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.06,
      "end": 175.1,
      "text": "or confidently repeat it."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.48,
      "end": 177.22,
      "text": "You need to judge which is happening."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.82,
      "end": 179.96,
      "text": "AI amplifies whatever you bring to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.36,
      "end": 182.2,
      "text": "Good thinking in, sharper output."
    }
